    "patched_vulnerabilities": [
      "All 162 CVE-2026 identifiers on Apple's iOS 27 page are listed here. Its kernel-memory entries: 2 write, 7 corruption, 8 read or disclosure, and 4 privilege. Calif.io-credited: 4 (one of them, CVE-2026-28968, a kernel corruption entry). 40 identifiers carry an 'Entry added' or 'Entry updated' note dated 2026-10-19 or 2026-10-26. Details: research/apple-27x-cve-mapping.md."
    ],
    "relevant_kernel_changes": "Apple's iOS 27 page lists the kernel entries above for iOS 27 and states no affected version range. Two entries (CVE-2026-84607 and CVE-2026-86916) are listed as arbitrary code execution with kernel privileges, CVE-2026-43689 as root privileges for a malicious app, and CVE-2026-84622 as a root-process read of uninitialised kernel memory (C-074). Some entries were added on 2026-10-26, so the page changed after the 27.0 release. Its notes do not say when a fix shipped in a given build (C-071). Build 24A446 is a later build; Apple's index lists no CVE entries for it (C-007).",
